---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import FactsRail from "../../components/FactsRail.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Now / Work · Sundharesan Kumaresan">
  <section class="relative left-1/2 right-1/2 -mx-[50vw] w-screen overflow-hidden md:bg-fixed bg-cover bg-center" style="min-height:56vh; background-image: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(0,0,0,.72), rgba(0,0,0,.22) 60%, rgba(0,0,0,.42)), url('/img/work.jpg')">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-[1100px] flex-col justify-end px-6 pb-12" style="min-height:56vh; padding-top:2rem;">
      <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-stellar">The present</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-serif font-semibold leading-[0.95] text-white" style="font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6.5vw, 4rem);">Now</h1>
    </div>
  </section>
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-[1100px] px-6 py-16">
    <p data-reveal class="max-w-[24ch] font-serif font-semibold leading-[1.05]" style="font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);">Hand me a problem and a blank slate, and I get weirdly happy about it.</p>
    <div data-reveal class="mt-14 grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-[1.3fr_0.7fr]">
      <div class="max-w-[60ch] space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
        <p>&ldquo;Forward-deployed engineer&rdquo; is the title on paper. In practice: a client turns up with a problem and no plan, and somehow that becomes my week. I sit with them, real people and real conversations, sketch the fix on a whiteboard, draw the architecture, gently prove it isn&rsquo;t held together by hope, then go build the thing for real. Mostly AI. Then actual users get hold of it, and they turn out to be remarkably talented at breaking whatever I was proudest of.</p>
        <p>I&rsquo;m an early adopter to a fault. I&rsquo;ll try the shiny new model the week it drops, then spend the next one trying to break it myself, because benchmarks lie and trust is earned. New-age tools, old-school paranoia. Honestly, I treat every build like a story: a problem, some tension, a third act where it finally clicks. My whole job is getting us to that third act: fast, and ideally without the scene where everything&rsquo;s on fire.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:border-l md:border-border md:pl-10 md:sticky md:top-28 md:self-start">
        <FactsRail items={[
          { label: "Role", value: "Forward-deployed engineer (professional problem-haver) · Oogway Labs" },
          { label: "What I build", value: "AI, end to end: from “what if” to “wait, it actually scales”" },
          { label: "How I work", value: "Move fast, break my own ideas first, keep what survives" },
        ]} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
